            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for an oath (formal), then the Hindi for bound (by a rule or a time)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: क़िस्मत",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क़िस्मत — qismat — \"luck; fortune\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उसकी क़िस्मत अच्छी है, उसे हमेशा सीट मिल जाती है। Uskī qismat acchī hai, use hameśā sīṭ mil jātī hai. He is lucky: he always gets a seat."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "क़िस्मत (qismat) is usually traced to Arabic qisma, \"a share, a portion\", through Persian. One's share, handed out in advance, is one's luck."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
