          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दाँव — dā̃v — \"a turn (in a game); a stake\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अगर इस बार मेरा दाँव लग गया, तो मैं जीत जाऊँगा। Agar is bār merā dā̃v lag gayā, to maiṁ jīt jāūṅgā. If my luck holds this time, I will win."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दाँव (dā̃v) लगना: one's turn or one's gamble comes off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दाँव (dā̃v) is a tadbhava, inherited from Sanskrit dātu, \"a share\" (CDIAL 6258). CDIAL gives the Hindi word as \"a turn\": one's share of the play."
            }
          ]
        },
